4/321994/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ic785f9f3c677bea997d4637266c8c223618070d9" commit="e6420a9304ea558079b1d2fa03a152e561f1595e" commit_message="[autotest] Change DB update order.  Originally, we update shard DBs first and then the master DB, and use the shard DB as ground truth when inconsistency between the master DB and a shard DB is detected. This incurs a tricky bug as explained in crbug.com/574966.  We should change the order. Update the master DB first and then shard DBs, and use the master DB as ground truth for fixing DB inconsistency.  BUG=chromium:574966 TEST=Test updated RPCs in puppylab.  Change-Id: Ic785f9f3c677bea997d4637266c8c223618070d9 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/320599 Commit-Ready: Mungyung Ryu &lt;mkryu@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Mungyung Ryu &lt;mkryu@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Dan Shi &lt;dshi@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="4" gerrit_number="320599" owner_email="mkryu@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/99/320599/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="4"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I289b2c85430cf134050dfea6d0ca4f2f190600d2" commit="cbf034eb71d1ff3ffd8424a134dc5ab15f36f629" commit_message="Enable virtual versions &gt;= 4  In some cases we may need to have virtual versions &gt;= 4, such as if there is a board which inherits another board overlay. This adjusts the pre-upload script to allow for these.  BUG=None TEST=Try uploading a CL with a virtual that is version 4.  Change-Id: I289b2c85430cf134050dfea6d0ca4f2f190600d2 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/321724 Commit-Ready: Bernie Thompson &lt;bhthompson@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Bernie Thompson &lt;bhthompson@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="321724" owner_email="bhthompson@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/repohooks" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/repohooks" ref="refs/changes/24/321724/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I464ae11b86078c34223a11224349db33b306726f" commit="11ec3f2d8ef326e67612d3c92bbba3e9c395eea8" commit_message="brillo_Gtest: Allows running tests as shell.  Some tests don't want to be run as root. This CL updates the format of the test whitelist to add a &quot;run as root&quot; option. If this option is not yes, the tests are run as user shell.  Bug: 25186790 Test: `./test_droid.py emulator-5554 brillo_WhitelistedGtests`.   libbrillo_test succeeds.  Change-Id: I464ae11b86078c34223a11224349db33b306726f Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/321970 Commit-Ready: Bertrand Simonnet &lt;bsimonnet@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Bertrand Simonnet &lt;bsimonnet@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Ari Hausman-Cohen &lt;arihc@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="321970" owner_email="bsimonnet@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/70/321970/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ibb7f3e8a03a64760758ceb29b0ac742ad0c9f3db" commit="84aa8be6fa19f3eec80ec5221c07d4e983d82249" commit_message="Increase time allowed for servod to start in deployment_test.  Sometimes, the &quot;deployment_test&quot; script fails with &quot;Connection refused&quot; from the servo.  Looking at the logs, there doesn't seem to be anything wrong with the servo as such, but it's possible that we're not allowing servod enough time to get started.  This increases the time allowance from 4 seconds to 10 seconds.  BUG=chromium:577324 TEST=None  Change-Id: Ibb7f3e8a03a64760758ceb29b0ac742ad0c9f3db Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/321950 Commit-Ready: Richard Barnette &lt;jrbarnette@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Richard Barnette &lt;jrbarnette@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dan Shi &lt;dshi@google.com&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="321950" owner_email="jrbarnette@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/50/321950/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ie561bbde3035e71c9bef8a422d6d065f01235fef" commit="9dc88748c595d8c317c783343663647d3550164f" commit_message="Change _servo_repair_power() to use cold reset.  Cold reset slightly improves the odds of success because it also resets the EC.  BUG=chromium:577284 TEST=None  Change-Id: Ie561bbde3035e71c9bef8a422d6d065f01235fef Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/321408 Commit-Ready: Richard Barnette &lt;jrbarnette@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Richard Barnette &lt;jrbarnette@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Paul Hobbs &lt;phobbs@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Kevin Cheng &lt;kevcheng@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="3" gerrit_number="321408" owner_email="jrbarnette@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/08/321408/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="3"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Ie625f2f91ea8897b5a19d070961ec7881eabf4e3" commit="1fb9c987b5a90730a2bc49067350d5caed3af34e" commit_message="UPSTREAM: drm/i915: Restore inhibiting the load of the default context  Following a GPU reset, we may leave the context in a poorly defined state, and reloading from that context will leave the GPU flummoxed. For secondary contexts, this will lead to that context being banned - but currently it is also causing the default context to become banned, leading to turmoil in the shared state.  This is a regression from  commit 6702cf16e0ba8b0129f5aa1b6609d4e9c70bc13b [v4.1] Author: Ben Widawsky &lt;benjamin.widawsky@intel.com&gt; Date:   Mon Mar 16 16:00:58 2015 +0000      drm/i915: Initialize all contexts  which quietly introduced the removal of the MI_RESTORE_INHIBIT on the default context.  v2: Mark the global default context as uninitialized on GPU reset so that the context-local workarounds are reloaded upon re-enabling.  Signed-off-by: Chris Wilson &lt;chris@chris-wilson.co.uk&gt; Cc: Michel Thierry &lt;michel.thierry@intel.com&gt; Cc: Mika Kuoppala &lt;mika.kuoppala@intel.com&gt; Cc: Daniel Vetter &lt;daniel.vetter@ffwll.ch&gt; Link: http://patchwork.freedesktop.org/patch/msgid/1448630935-27377-1-git-send-email-chris@chris-wilson.co.uk Reviewed-by: Mika Kuoppala &lt;mika.kuoppala@intel.com&gt; Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org [danvet: This seems to fix a gpu hand on after the first resume, resulting in any future suspend operation failing with -EIO because the gpu seems to be in a funky state. Somehow this patch fixes that.] Signed-off-by: Daniel Vetter &lt;daniel.vetter@ffwll.ch&gt; (cherry picked from commit 42f1cae8c079bcceb3cff079fddc3ff8852c788f git://anongit.freedesktop.org/drm-intel drm-intel-nightly) Signed-off-by: Kalyan Kondapally &lt;kalyan.kondapally@intel.com&gt;  BUG=chrome-os-partner:48349 TEST=Ensure No graphic regressions found after system boots. TEST=Ensure playing Video using HWA VP9 Decoding and launching camera      same time doesn't cause the camera stream to get corrupted.  Change-Id: Ie625f2f91ea8897b5a19d070961ec7881eabf4e3 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/321200 Commit-Ready: Marc Herbert &lt;marc.herbert@intel.com&gt; Tested-by: Russ Sage &lt;russ.sage@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="321200" owner_email="kalyan.kondapally@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/00/321200/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I1f9ed2a74db0aa6b04e359e9ef6c1cf088f66f13" commit="2ba15e244b575eb55296acdbb245aa8a936cff7d" commit_message="frecon: move all terminal management to term.c from input.c  And related cleanups and removal of unused functions and declarations. BUG=none TEST=run frecon on daisy spring  Change-Id: I1f9ed2a74db0aa6b04e359e9ef6c1cf088f66f13 Signed-off-by: Dominik Behr &lt;dbehr@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/321931 Reviewed-by: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="321931" owner_email="dbehr@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/frecon" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/frecon" ref="refs/changes/31/321931/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2015.07" change_id="I09e1ce1a45a217afc88f422cf7db7924fad6b6f9" commit="247db807782efacd3efd4f3b29ae6e1104e78008" commit_message="chell: Add new memory part for DVT build  After comparing datasheets it appears to have the same geometry and timings as the K4E6E304EE-EGCF part with just a new part number.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:49357 BRANCH=glados TEST=build and boot on chell EVT (new part is not used until DVT)  Change-Id: I09e1ce1a45a217afc88f422cf7db7924fad6b6f9 Signed-off-by: Duncan Laurie &lt;dlaurie@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/321956 Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="321956" owner_email="dlaurie@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/56/321956/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ifa